# Closing issues from PRs

When opening or updating a pull request that is meant to finish specific GitHub issues/tickets, include GitHub closing keywords in the PR description so merge auto-closes them.

## Required form

Use one `closes` per issue, comma-separated:

```text
closes #1, closes #2
```

Put that line near the top of the PR body (after a one-line summary is fine). Do not rely on plain references like `Implements #1` or `Part of #2` alone when the PR is intended to close those tickets.

## Scope

- Include every issue this PR fully completes.
- Omit parent epics or tracking issues that still have unfinished work.
- Omit issues that are only related context, not done by this PR.
- If the PR later grows to finish more tickets, update the description to add the matching `closes #N` entries.
